# Run artifacts. Each run's debug/delegations/ is its OWN git repository
# (spec 11: one commit per delegation), so this is not merely noise-filtering:
# without it a `git add -A` here would absorb that nested repo as a gitlink
# and commit a broken submodule reference into adda.
studies/*/runs/

# A study's outputs. runs/ is above; these are the rest of what a run writes
# into the study dir. The one thing kept from workspace/ is the oracle the
# study is DEFINED by -- everything else there is written by the agents, which
# is what a workspace is for (studies/example_study is the reference layout:
# PROBLEM_STATEMENT.md + config.yaml + run.py + workspace/evaluator.py).
studies/*/workspace/*
!studies/*/workspace/evaluator.py
studies/*/surrogates/
studies/*/pipeline*.ipynb
studies/*/*.log
studies/*/test_summary.json
